% ============================================================================
% days-of-week.query.adj — a worked recall over the calendar facts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what number is Monday?": it
% states no calendar fact — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding
% queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `iso_weekday` rows and returns
% the number + the table's source/locator/trust. The query runs in reverse too
% (number → day). Anything that is not a day of the week abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents a weekday number.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli days-of-week.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "days-of-week.adj"

? iso_weekday(monday, $N)        % expect 1
? iso_weekday(sunday, $N)        % expect 7
? iso_weekday($Day, 1)           % expect monday — reverse lookup, "which day is 1?"
? iso_weekday(funday, $N)        % expect abstain — funday is not a day of the week
